    {
      "id": "s01-flow",
      "intent": "The four stages, and the recurrence that returns to the third",
      "claim": "Thought happens inside one stage, not around the whole flow",
      "narration": "An image enters, is encoded into a dense feature field, and is cut into windows. The third stage runs the thought process, and the recurrence returns to that stage itself. Every tick reuses the same parameters, so depth costs time rather than weights. Decoding turns the finished tokens back into pixels.",
